    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0164" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg70"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January 6,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1385.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 2645, of November 24 last, inclosing copy of the note which, in compliance
                    with the Department’s instructions, you sent to the Tsung-li Yamên demanding the
                    punishment of officials who failed to do their duty in the protection of
                    American citizens at Kutien, and also damages for Miss Hartford.</p>
                <p>You will urge on the Yamên the necessity of prompt action.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
